Many problems show an error message in the console window. Keep it open and read it.

## Common problems

**Windows or your antivirus blocks the file.** For files from the [official releases](https://github.com/LostRuins/koboldcpp/releases/latest) this is a false alarm: the file is not signed. Click **More info**, then **Run anyway**, or allow the file in your antivirus. [More](/docs/install/windows/#smartscreen-and-antivirus-warnings)

**The window closes straight away.** Start KoboldCpp from a Command Prompt (Windows) or a terminal, so the error stays on screen. On an older PC, try the `oldpc` file. [More](/docs/troubleshooting/wont-start/)

**"Out of memory", or a crash while loading.** Pick a smaller model or the `LowSpec` template, and close other programs that use the graphics card. [More](/docs/troubleshooting/out-of-memory/)

**Replies are very slow.** Check that **Backend:** on **Quick Launch** shows **Use CUDA** (NVIDIA) or **Use Vulkan** (AMD, Intel), not **Use CPU**. If **Use CUDA** is missing on an NVIDIA PC, you have the `nocuda` file; [download](/download/) `koboldcpp.exe` instead. [More](/docs/troubleshooting/gpu-and-speed/)

**The model doesn't load.** Use one `.gguf` file, and download it again if the download was cut short. Newer model types need the latest KoboldCpp. [More](/docs/troubleshooting/model-wont-load/)

**Nothing happens on macOS.** Run it from Terminal as shown in [Start KoboldCpp](/getting-started/start/), and allow it in **System Settings → Privacy & Security**. [More](/docs/install/macos/)

## Ask for help

Ask on the [KoboldAI Discord](https://koboldai.org/discord) or in [GitHub Discussions](https://github.com/LostRuins/koboldcpp/discussions). Found a bug? [Report it on GitHub](https://github.com/LostRuins/koboldcpp/issues). Copy the error from the console window into your message.

